# The header names both sides, and for a tracker that is a directory the right-hand one is the
# working tree — the files as they stand, committed or not. That is the whole question `diff`
# with no `--to` answers, so the label has to say it.
#
# Pinned because the other kind of tracker cannot say it: read out of a git ref there is no
# working tree to compare against, and the label there is the ref. Two spellings of one line,
# and this is the one a fixture can state — a ref-backed tracker needs a git repository, which
# this suite deliberately does not build.
#
# `--from` rather than a bare `trck diff`: the default left side is `HEAD`, which invokes git,
# and there is none here.
